Let $A$ and $B$ be subsets of a declared universe $U$. Then:

- $A\cup B:=\{x\in U:x\in A\lor x\in B\}$;
- $A\cap B:=\{x\in U:x\in A\land x\in B\}$;
- $A\setminus B:=\{x\in U:x\in A\land x\notin B\}$.

The complement of $A$ is written $U\setminus A$. Keeping $U$ visible prevents the same set from acquiring different complements when the surrounding discussion changes.
